Midnight
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/relay_post]

FIXME(dread): The post is very quiet. Devra is at her desk in the lamp-light. The storeroom door is closed; Ossal is asleep on the cot inside. The wire ticks once in its cradle and stops. You are in the chair against the wall under the blanket Devra gave you.

choices:

* Hear Devra out = She crosses the floor and crouches by your chair [requires !tag relay_post.devra_asked]
    FIXME(dread): Devra crosses the floor and crouches at your chair. She glances once at the storeroom door. She speaks low so as not to wake Ossal. She is leaving at first light. Not back to the capital. To Aldgate. She cannot keep filing orders she believes are coming from something inhuman. She cannot keep feeding messages to settlements when she does not know which are administrative and which are something else wearing the shape of administration.
    FIXME(dread): She wants a letter of introduction from you to the guild chapter in Aldgate. You are a guild member. A sealed letter with your credential would get her through the gate as something other than a Kesharat deserter. She is not asking you to endorse her theory. She is asking for a piece of paper. She will do the rest.
    FIXME(revelation): She tells you something she has not told Ossal. She has been keeping copies of the anomalous messages. Actual duplicates of the original transcriptions, hidden in her pack. If the orders are coming from the Lattice, those copies are evidence. She wants to put them in front of someone outside the Kesharat system who can evaluate them clean.
    +add_tag relay_post.devra_asked
    +add_tag relay_post.kept_copies
    +open "Midnight"

* Hear Ossal out = The storeroom door opens and he beckons you in [requires tag relay_post.devra_asked && !tag relay_post.ossal_asked]
    FIXME(mundane): The storeroom door opens. Ossal stands in the gap fully dressed; he was not asleep. He beckons you in with a small gesture. You follow him. He closes the door behind you and stands with his back against it. The room is small. There is a cot, a lamp, a stack of supply crates. Devra cannot hear you in here.
    FIXME(dread): Ossal does not mention the Lattice. He chooses his words precisely. Devra is a state employee with access to classified communications. She is clearly disloyal. She has been keeping unauthorized copies of official documents. If she deserts the post, the settlements downstream lose their only relay. Supply orders. Medical requests. Patrol coordination. Real people, real consequences.
    FIXME(dread): He asks you to help him detain her until a patrol arrives. He is too old to confront her alone. With your help he could secure the post, confiscate the copies, keep the relay running until a replacement comes. 
    FIXME(revelation): He also alludes to her mental wellbeing. She's been isolated out here for who knows how long. She's likely imagining stories to pass the time, or simply hallucinating under the strain. If word got out, it could alarm ordinary people. It could tarnish the reputation of the Kesharat. There's already wild rumors about his people; this will only make things worse.
    FIXME(mundane): He opens the door and you return to your chair. Devra looks up from her desk. She does not ask what was said.
    +add_tag relay_post.ossal_asked
    +open "Midnight"

* Write the letter for Devra = Sit down at the desk with a pen [requires tag relay_post.devra_asked]
    FIXME(action): You take a clean sheet from Devra's stack. You write the letter in guild form. To the Aldgate chapter, the bearer of this letter to be received and given shelter. The writing takes five minutes. You melt wax from the desk lamp and press your seal. You hand her the folded paper. She holds it for a long moment before tucking it into her coat.
    FIXME(mundane): You go back to your chair. Devra packs her bag at her desk: spare clothes, food rations, the wax-paper sleeve of duplicate transcriptions. She works quietly. You doze in pieces. The storm outside has dropped to a low wind. Hours pass. The lamp burns down. The first gray of dawn shows in the high window.
    +open "Dawn Devra"

* Help Ossal secure the post = Tell Ossal quietly you are with him [requires tag relay_post.ossal_asked]
    FIXME(action): When Ossal next opens the storeroom door you give him a small nod. He nods back. The two of you agree without words: you will move at first light, when Devra cannot slip out into the dark with the sleeve. Until then you wait.
    FIXME(mundane): You sit up the rest of the night. Ossal sits up with you. Devra works at her desk and does not look at either of you. The storm outside has dropped to a low wind. The lamp burns down. The first gray of dawn shows in the high window. Ossal gets up from the storeroom doorway, pours himself a cup of tea from the brazier pot, and takes a position where he can see Devra's desk and the back door at once. He looks at you and waits.
    +open "Dawn Ossal"

* Decline both and wait for dawn = Stay in your chair and say nothing
    FIXME(mundane): You shake your head at Ossal. You shake your head at Devra. Neither presses you. They retreat to their corners. The post is silent. The wire is silent. Both of them are awake. Neither of them speaks to you or to each other.
    FIXME(mundane): You doze in pieces against the wall. The storm outside has dropped to a low wind. Hours pass. The lamp burns down. The first gray of dawn shows in the high window.
    +open "Dawn Refuse"
